#> pause: 40
#> must: 3 cherries 7 (no a)
#> must: 8 lemons 22 (no a)
#> must: 1 apples 12
#> not: 1 apples 12 (
#> source: /a/b
# 11. b. Sheet: "b label" branches to the label; with no label, to the end of the script.
# Lines that contain an a branch straight to the end and are printed unchanged.
# The others fall through to the s///, which tags them. Same as /a/!s/$/ (no a)/,
# but b scales: everything below it is skipped, however many commands there are.
# Try: put ":tag" on a line above the s and change b to "b tag": now every line is tagged.
/a/b
s/$/ (no a)/

